# Build context exclusions.
#
# Two of these are correctness, not speed:
#
#   * `db.sqlite*` — the working database, ~4MB of real internal corporate content
#     (see .gitignore). Copying it into the image would bake a snapshot of live data
#     into an artifact that gets pushed to a registry, and it would then shadow
#     nothing and confuse everything, since the container reads /data instead.
#   * `.env` — real provider API keys and the SharePoint client secret. An image
#     layer is not a secret store; anyone who can pull the image can read it.
#
# The rest is context size. `node_modules/` in particular must be excluded: it
# holds a better-sqlite3 addon compiled for the *host*, and copying it in would
# shadow the one the build compiles for the image's Node.

node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

db.sqlite
db.sqlite-wal
db.sqlite-shm
db.sqlite.bak*

.git/
.github/
.husky/
.claude/
.ai/

docs/screenshots/
tests/
# The eval corpus is test data and is excluded for context size — EXCEPT the
# three result files that src/constants/evalResults.ts imports, which Vite bundles
# into the frontend at `npm run build`. Excluding the whole directory made the
# Docker image build fail ("Could not resolve ../../eval/baseline.json") while a
# host build passed, because the file was in the working tree but not the context.
eval/
!eval/baseline.json
!eval/kb-test-set-a-results.json
!eval/kb-test-set-b-results.json
*.log
.DS_Store

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
deploy/
